WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.820
Roller Games, stop the most barbaric crime wave on ball bearings.

00:00:21.180 --> 00:00:22.020
Roller Games

00:00:22.020 --> 00:00:29.960
And welcome to NEStalgia, a chronological exploration of every NES game released in North America.

00:00:30.160 --> 00:00:32.060
I'm Mike. And I'm Sean.

00:00:33.940 --> 00:00:37.440
Roller Games for the uninformed, which would have included myself.

00:00:37.440 --> 00:00:39.760
I don't know about you, Sean. Were you informed about this beforehand?

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:46.260
This is just an amazing discovery I think we've made here.

00:00:46.520 --> 00:00:52.880
Okay, great. Because I think everybody who was alive for it probably buried it in their subconscious as well.

00:00:52.880 --> 00:01:01.980
So we're all going to awaken and remind ourselves that roller games was an actual television sport that debuted in 1989.

00:01:02.380 --> 00:01:05.760
Sport entertainment. Well, yeah, don't bury the lead.

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:12.940
It was a televised sport with a more theatrical take on roller derby.

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:18.460
There was a, like a figure eight track and modified rules.

00:01:18.460 --> 00:01:25.260
And there were teams, the T-Birds, the Violators, the Maniacs, a team just called Bad Attitude.

