A binary opinion. At the end of the episode, we'll just give like a score?

00:03:26.000 --> 00:03:27.120
Yeah, yeah, yeah. We'll give it a score. Out of a thousand?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:29.060
Out of whatever you want.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.760
Out of a thousand seems fair.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:32.280
This way we can do it. You can do it out of a thousand.

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:33.260
I'll do it out of something else.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.320
Okay, cool. Yeah, that way they'll know, you know, like, oh, that's the Sean scale.

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:38.420
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:45.100
Yep. What's funny is, as I was looking up stuff about roller games, obviously I start with the video game because I don't think it's based on anything.

00:03:45.100 --> 00:03:51.100
Then I find out it's based on this sport, and I'm just reading about the sport, and this caught my eye.

00:03:51.560 --> 00:03:52.820
Bill Griffith Sr.

00:03:53.300 --> 00:03:54.280
was the commissioner.

00:03:54.720 --> 00:03:59.380
Uh-huh. So I'm looking at the list of the teams and their managers, and Bill Griffith Jr.

00:04:00.400 --> 00:04:07.220
Is the manager of the Los Angeles T-Birds, and I say, wait a minute, that sounds like a conflict of interest.

00:04:07.220 --> 00:04:17.460
And all of that, all of those fears were put to rest when I finally just said, well, I just need to see how this show even went down.

00:04:18.040 --> 00:04:26.380
And man, am I glad that we have the Griffiths to save us from the likes of the violators led by the evil skull.

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:29.900
Mr. Mean. Yeah, you're right, you're right.

00:04:30.820 --> 00:04:33.320
There's just so much, like, this is peak 80s.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:47.040
Like, this is, I know that there's, like, you know, also American Gladiator to think about the shows like this, but, like, when I turned this TV show on, it was just like you are immersed in it.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:05:04.720
Like, I thought that if I looked out my window, I would see, like, I would see, like, Marlboro ads everywhere and just every person walking down the sidewalk to have some really, like, hair sprayed out, like, feathered shit going on.

00:05:04.840 --> 00:05:06.280
Like, I thought I was there.

00:05:06.620 --> 00:05:07.840
Like, this is so good.

00:05:08.740 --> 00:05:15.460
And you mentioned wrestling as another form of sports entertainment, and you just brought up American Gladiator.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:22.380
Those two, and specifically wrestling, like, wrestling will have, you know, funny characters, right?

00:05:22.540 --> 00:05:30.600
People that have, like, either a quirky personality to them or kind of a gimmick about them.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:44.460
But for the most part, like, the really strong macho guy is usually the one fighting the other really strong macho guy for the, you know, the world championship, the thing that, like, has it all on the line.

00:05:45.520 --> 00:05:49.840
That is not true in roller games, and I knew that the second I saw the teams come out.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.700
These people, first off, there are people on the team that are, like, 70 years old.

00:05:54.240 --> 00:05:55.700
Well, those are the OGs.

00:05:55.740 --> 00:05:56.700
Those are the OGs roller.

00:05:56.960 --> 00:06:01.080
Because apparently roller games was also a thing in, like, the 60s and stuff.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:04.280
