00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.960
They don't look like they got the cream of the crop.

00:06:11.520 --> 00:06:20.920
Yeah. Just to keep going on the show, like, this looks like a sport that they just pulled people off the street to play.

00:06:20.920 --> 00:06:43.620
Like, I think regardless of whether you follow hockey or football or soccer, like, you can, there's, like, an, there's a subconscious, like, oh, wow, these people make the bodily movements that they're doing look good and measured and graceful in some capacity.

00:06:43.620 --> 00:06:47.740
Like, it looks like they are executing something athletically.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:50.440
That is not what's happening here.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:52.180
When you watch these people.

00:06:52.440 --> 00:06:54.160
Is this even roller derby?

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.080
Like, I've never seen roller derby.

00:06:56.280 --> 00:06:59.200
But this is some sort of offshoot of roller derby.

00:06:59.300 --> 00:07:00.500
It's so funny.

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:04.380
Yeah, this is definitely different than roller derby.

00:07:04.500 --> 00:07:11.460
Because, remember, roller derby, like, the real stuff doesn't traditionally have a wall of death or an alligator pit.

00:07:12.100 --> 00:07:15.320
Well, yeah, the wall of the alligator pit for sure.

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:18.240
Well, you know, I wouldn't be surprised.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:25.220
But, actually, I did go see an all-women's roller derby last time I was up in Buffalo.

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:30.260
