00:07:32.460 --> 00:07:36.420
I was just, like, at this, like, open space to drink.

00:07:37.340 --> 00:07:39.620
You know. Yeah, you were at Riverworks.

00:07:40.020 --> 00:07:40.820
Riverworks. Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:07:40.820 --> 00:07:43.700
I didn't want to, like, you know, I didn't want to, like, dox the bar.

00:07:45.340 --> 00:07:46.260
But that's a joke.

00:07:46.540 --> 00:07:49.500
But, you know, and I was watching it just, like, casually.

00:07:49.500 --> 00:07:51.600
And I was, like, wow, this is really exciting.

00:07:51.800 --> 00:07:56.380
Like, it's kind of weird that they saw roller derby and were, like, we need to amp this up.

00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:57.820
Like, we need to definitely dial this thing.

00:07:57.820 --> 00:07:58.740
Yeah, that was my thought.

00:07:58.880 --> 00:08:01.860
Like, I thought roller derby was already, like, amped up.

00:08:02.200 --> 00:08:03.380
Yeah, it's aggressive, too.

00:08:03.460 --> 00:08:04.300
It's very physical.

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:11.240
There are, like, you know, hip checks and, like, little tricks you can do to wipe out your opponent and stuff.

00:08:11.240 --> 00:08:12.480
So it's there.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:17.400
They just felt the need to take everything to the next level, including the personalities.

00:08:17.460 --> 00:08:22.240
These are, like, cartoonish levels of acting.

00:08:22.240 --> 00:08:23.180
So cartoonish. But, yeah.

00:08:23.700 --> 00:08:34.200
But, you know, it's also, like, they're just not convincing me the same way that, you know, like, Macho Man Randy Savage

00:08:34.200 --> 00:08:38.580
Right? Who, like, now is cartoonish by, like, the wrestlers we have.

00:08:38.940 --> 00:08:43.200
Right? Like, he was clearly, you know, just overdoing everything.

00:08:43.260 --> 00:08:46.080
But, like, back then that was, like, yeah, I want to be Macho Man.

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:47.620
I still want to be Macho Man.

00:08:48.020 --> 00:08:51.320
Well, yeah. I would love to just wake up tomorrow and be Macho Man.

00:08:51.500 --> 00:08:53.800
Yeah. Mostly for the Slim Jim endorsement.

00:08:55.780 --> 00:08:59.920
But, you know, I guess what I'm trying to say is, like, and this is probably true in many sports,

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:05.360
but, like, the cheerleaders look like they are in better shape than everyone who's on the field.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:15.320
That's true. And I do like that they all get their themed cheerleaders, even though I think you called one of the teams the Los Angeles T-Birds.

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:17.080
I think they're all Los Angeles, by the way.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:18.280
Yeah, I don't know why I did that.

00:09:18.760 --> 00:09:20.960
I think that was from, that was a Wikipedia leftover.

00:09:20.960 --> 00:09:33.600
But I appreciate that they are so themed that, like, even the cheerleaders will, like, get into the fights on the court, the field, the track.

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:50.540
Like, their managers are, like, a heartless entertainment lawyer and some kind of weird biker gang, I guess.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:55.340
Not even just a biker gang leader, but he's a, okay.

00:09:55.340 --> 00:10:01.820
Okay. He worships a head in a box of some long dead god.

00:10:02.160 --> 00:10:05.500
I guess, like, did you see this in the...

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:07.960
Yeah, I mean, we saw the same episode, but, yeah, I don't know.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:09.640
I wouldn't know the word for that.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:11.340
I guess pagan. Pagan.

00:10:11.460 --> 00:10:25.260
There we go. But, you know, with all of these, like, not only are they so hyped up and everything, but it's also, like, it's just assumed on episode one, right?

00:10:25.340 --> 00:10:31.920
Of this brand new sport that, like, you would know the ins and outs and the storylines and the play.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.620
